# fixedbugs, defect 2036's finding, pinned 2026-10-13 as a known cost.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own whose `printf("a\0b%d\n", 5)` holds
# a `\0` inside its format is refused `ffi_header_refused` at exit 1, `format
# string contains '\0' within the string body [-Werror,-Wformat]`.
#
# REASON: C defines the call: a string ends at its first null character (C11
# 7.1.1p1), so the format is `a` and `5` an excess argument, evaluated and
# otherwise ignored (7.21.6.1p2); but clang files the diagnostic under
# `-Wformat` itself, under none of its parts, and the region keeps `-Wformat`
# an error for the conversion its argument does not match, which reads the
# wrong bytes (defect 2034); no pragma reaches one of its own diagnostics
# alone (`emit/header_region.hero`).
#
# RULING: the author's, 2026-10-13, a known cost: robustness first (design.md
# §1.12). Revisit if clang gives this diagnostic a flag of its own; this
# golden moves when the region can pass it over.

extern "fixedbugs-2036-a-header-s-printf-of-a-format-holding-a-nul-is-a-known-cost.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function fmt_shape() -> i32

function main()
    print(fmt_shape())
